Type `chat` to talk in #runv on tilde.chat, the IRC network the tilde
servers share. It opens senpai through our bouncer at irc.runv.club, so
you stay connected while you're away and catch up on what you missed.

The same account works in the browser at https://chat.runv.club and in
any client that speaks to a bouncer: irc.runv.club, port 6697, TLS, your
username, and the password in ~/.config/runv/irc-token. `runv token irc`
makes a new one.

Register your nick on tilde.chat so nobody else takes it:

  /msg NickServ REGISTER yourpassword you@example.org

Other networks (up to 3 in all) are added through BouncerServ:

  /msg BouncerServ network create -addr irc.libera.chat
  /msg BouncerServ help

Every network has its own rules and you're a guest there. If one of them
complains about you, the bouncer gets switched off for you.
tilde.chat's rules: https://tilde.wiki/Code_of_conduct

`chat weechat` skips the bouncer and opens weechat straight on tilde.chat.
